\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {5}{\ignorespaces Giver--recipient similarity relative to random pairing (the ratios in Table~\ref {tab:shared}). Diamonds compare the observed rate with random pairing within the same year; circles compare it with random pairing within the same branch and year. The distance between them is the part of the similarity explained by the office. Gray bars show the middle 95\% of the 500 branch-year permutations, so a circle outside its bar is unlikely to arise by chance. For a shared employer in the executive agencies, the bar extends below the axis because many permutations produce no matches.}}{16}{figure.caption.15}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:shared}{{5}{16}{Giver--recipient similarity relative to random pairing (the ratios in Table~\ref {tab:shared}). Diamonds compare the observed rate with random pairing within the same year; circles compare it with random pairing within the same branch and year. The distance between them is the part of the similarity explained by the office. Gray bars show the middle 95\% of the 500 branch-year permutations, so a circle outside its bar is unlikely to arise by chance. For a shared employer in the executive agencies, the bar extends below the axis because many permutations produce no matches}{figure.caption.15}{}}
